.TH EUCLID-CLI-EAP-LIST-EGRESS-SITES 1 "October 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-eap-list-egress-sites \- list each application's outside sites, egress limits and how they stand
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
.B eap list-egress-sites
[\fB\-\-application\-id\fR \fIid\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists, for each application in the caller's account and namespace,
every outside site it has asked an egress permit for or has a limit for,
with the limits it's held to and how it stands now. See
.BR euclid-cli-eap-set-egress-limit (1)
for what egress permits are. The caller must be an administrator.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-application\-id " " \fIid\fR
Only this application's sites.
.SH OUTPUT
The JSON response has
.I defaultLimits
(from
.IR euclid.modules.eap.egress.default )
and a
.I sites
array, sorted by application and site, each with:
.RS
.TP
.I applicationId
The application.
.TP
.I site
The host name, or
.I *
for the application's default for all its sites.
.TP
.I limits
.IR requestsPerSecond ", " burst " and " concurrent
in force for it.
.TP
.I limitsSet
.I true
if they were set for this entry with
.BR set-egress-limit ;
.I false
if they come from the application's
.I *
entry or from the default.
.PP
For a site (not for
.IR * ):
.TP
.I tokens
Requests that could start right now as far as the rate goes - up to the
burst.
.TP
.I inFlight
Permits held: the application's requests to the site that have started
and not finished. Includes those of an instance that died, until their
lease runs out.
.TP
.I blockedUntil
When the site asked the application to stay away (a 429 or 503 it
reported) and nothing is granted until then; empty if it isn't blocked.
.TP
.I lastUsed
When the application last asked for, or gave back, a permit for it.
.RE
.SH EXAMPLE
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli eap list-egress-sites --application-id downloader
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-eap (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eap-set-egress-limit (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eap-delete-egress-limit (1)
